                                                                   528 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 2 Revision, July 2000, S. Frankle, J. Campbell,     528 1451
                 R. Little (LANL)                                  528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
   The evaluation was modified so that the threshold for the       528 1451
 (n,n'continuum) reaction, MT=91, was the same for the secondary   528 1451
 particle production as for the cross section. The threshold for   528 1451
 the secondary neutrons and photons was changed from 1.050000e+7   528 1451
 to 1.002700e+7 eV.                                                528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 Covariances were estimated at LANL based on a brief analysis      528 1451
 of experimental data and their agreement with the ENDF/B-VII.0    528 1451
 central values.                                                   528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 ***************************************************************** 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, P.G. Young (LANL) May 1989            528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 GENERAL DESCRIPTION                                               528 1451
   This evaluation is a synthesis of experimental results and      528 1451
 theoretical calculations using the GNASH Hauser-Feshbach,         528 1451
 statistical theory code [ar88, yo77]. It replaces a pre-1970 U.K. 528 1451
 evaluation that was adapted for ENDF/B in 1971 [co79].            528 1451
   Major emphasis was placed on experimental data where possible,  528 1451
 usually using the calculations to estimate shapes and             528 1451
 experimental data to normalize the the calculations. Spherical    528 1451
 optical model calculations were used to obtain particle           528 1451
 transmission coefficients, using global potentials for protons    528 1451
 and alphas, and the work of Dave et al. [Da83] for the neutron    528 1451
 potential.  Gilbert-Cameron level density parameters were used    528 1451
 and preequilibrium corrections from an exciton model were         528 1451
 included. In general, the calculations were required for the      528 1451
 gamma and particle emission spectra from charged-particle         528 1451
 reactions, as well as for inelastic neutron and gamma emission    528 1451
 above the third excited state of B11, and for all states above    528 1451
 an incident neutron energy of about 8 MeV.                        528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=2 RESONANCE PARAMETERS *************************************** 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MT=151  scattering radius only.                                   528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=3 SMOOTH NEUTRON CROSS SECTIONS ****************************** 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 THERMAL CROSS SECTIONS                                            528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
   The 1981 evaluation by Mughabghab [mu81] was used for the       528 1451
 2200 m/s cross sections, as follows:                              528 1451
         MT =  1   sigma = 4.8455 b                                528 1451
         MT =  2   sigma = 4.8400 b                                528 1451
         MT =102   sigma = 0.0055 b                                528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MT=  1  Total Cross Section. At low energies, evaluation by Mu81a 528 1451
         of thermal data used.  At higher energies exp. data of    528 1451
         Mo66, La70, Ca73, Au79, Co52 & Co54 were used. The high   528 1451
         resolution data of Au79 were emphasized.  Optical model   528 1451
         calculations with the Da83 potential used to define shape 528 1451
         above 14 MeV.                                             528 1451
 MT=  2  Elastic Cross Section.  Based on exp. data of La70,       528 1451
         Wi55, Po70, Ne73, Wh80, Ko82, Ho69, Gl82, Co70 & Al69.    528 1451
         Optical model calculations with potential of Da83         528 1451
         used with renormalization above 14 MeV. Thermal eval.     528 1451
         of Mu81a used at low energies.                            528 1451
 MT=  4  (n,nprime)gamma+(n,nprime)continuum. sum of mt=51-60,91.  528 1451
 MT= 16  (n,2n) Cross Section.  Based entirely on GNASH analysis.  528 1451
 MT= 22  (n,na) Cross Section.  Based entirely on GNASH analysis.  528 1451
 MT= 28  (n,np) Cross Section.  Based entirely on GNASH analysis.  528 1451
 MT=51-54 (n,n'gamma) Cross Sections. Based on exp. data of        528 1451
         Au86, Gl82, Ho69, Po70, Co70, Ko82, Ba85. The Au86 data   528 1451
         shapes were used to establish low energy behavior.        528 1451
 MT=55-60 (n,n'gamma) Cross Sections. Shapes of excitation         528 1451
         curves calculated with GNASH. Absolute magnitudes obtain- 528 1451
         ed by renormalizing such that sum of all partials gave    528 1451
         reaction, elastic, total x/s consistent with avail. data. 528 1451
 MT= 91  (n,n'continuum) Cross Section. Based on GNASH calculation 528 1451
         entirely.                                                 528 1451
 MT=102  (n,gamma) Cross Section.  adopted from endf/b-v.1 except  528 1451
         thermal cross section of Mu81a used.                      528 1451
 MT=103  (n,p) Cross Section.  Based on GNASH calculation and exp. 528 1451
         data of Sc70a,Fl67, St65, etc.                            528 1451
 MT=105  (n,t) Cross Section. Similar to endf/b-v data, with a     528 1451
         smooth curve passing thru exp. data of Wy58 at 14.1 MeV.  528 1451
 MT=107  (n,alpha) Cross Section.  Based on GNASH calculation and  528 1451
         exp. data (An79, Sc70b,Ar56).                             528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=4 NEUTRON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ****************************** 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MT=  2  legendre coefficients obtained by drawing smooth curve    528 1451
         through fitted coefficients from measurements listed      528 1451
         under mf3/mt2. data of La60,Gl79,Wh80,Ne73,Ho69,Hy74      528 1451
         emphasized. optical model calculations used above 14 mev. 528 1451
 MT=51-54 Legendre coefficients obtained by fitting exp.data,      528 1451
         especially Al69, Hy74, Po70, Ho69, Gl79 & Co69. Smooth    528 1451
         curves then passed through fitted coefficients.           528 1451
 MT=55-60  Isotropy assumed.                                       528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=6 ENERGY-ANGLE CORRELATED DISTRIBUTIONS ********************** 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MT= 16  Neutron and photon distributions are given based on       528 1451
         GNASH calculations described above to obtain spectra      528 1451
         and multiplicities. Kalbach-Mann (Ka81) systematics (KMS) 528 1451
         used for neutron angular distributions. Photon distri-    528 1451
         butions taken as isotropic.                               528 1451
 MT= 22  Neutron and alpha distributions are based on KMS.         528 1451
         Photon distributions assumed isotropic. Multiplicities    528 1451
         and spectra based on GNASH calculations.                  528 1451
 MT= 28  Neutron and proton distributions are based on KMS.        528 1451
         Photon distributions assumed isotropic. Multiplicities    528 1451
         and spectra based on GNASH calculations.                  528 1451
 MT= 91  Neutron distributions based on KMS and isotropic photon   528 1451
         distributions given. Multiplicities and spectra obtained  528 1451
         from GNASH analysis.                                      528 1451
 MT=103  Proton distributions based on KMS and isotropic photon    528 1451
         distributions given. Multiplicities and spectra obtained  528 1451
         from GNASH analysis.                                      528 1451
 MT=107  Alpha distributions based on KMS and isotropic photon     528 1451
         distributions given. Multiplicities and spectra obtained  528 1451
         from GNASH analysis.                                      528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=13 PHOTON CROSS SECTIONS ************************************* 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MT=  4  gamma ray production cross sections from inelastic scat.  528 1451
         Obtained using discrete data (MF=3, MT=51-60) and photon  528 1451
         branching ratios (Aj85).                                  528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=14 PHOTON ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ****************************** 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MT= 51  isotropy assumed at all energies.                         528 1451
 MT=102  isotropy assumed for all gammas at all energies.          528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
 MF=33 NEUTRON CROSS SECTION COVARIANCES ************************* 528 1451
                                                                   528 1451
           To be provided in the future.                           528 1451
